 "intro_html": "Korean candied fried chicken. The drumsticks get an egg, flour and starch coat and are <b>fried twice</b>, so they stay crunchy under the glaze. The sauce is ginger slices boiled in soy, brown sugar and vinegar, then thickened with <b>corn syrup</b> until it’s sticky. The ginger candies in the syrup. Maangchi makes this with 40 wing pieces; these are drumsticks of the same weight, so her amounts stay as written.",
