 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Maangchi uses 40 wing pieces (about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"kg\" data-a=\"1.8\" data-s=\"0\">1.8 kg</span>).</li><li>12 drumsticks weigh about the same, so every batter and sauce amount is hers as written.</li><li><b>Changed for drumsticks:</b> the slashes to the bone (her own advice for drumsticks in her spicy BBQ chicken) and the first fry, which is longer and a little cooler (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"170\" data-s=\"0\">170 °C</span>, 12–15 min instead of her <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"175\" data-b=\"190\" data-s=\"0\">175–190 °C</span>) so the thick meat cooks through before the coat gets dark.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Drumsticks instead of wings"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Chicken is safe at <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"74\" data-s=\"0\">74 °C</span></b>.</li><li>Drumsticks are juicier at <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"temp\" data-u=\"C\" data-a=\"80\" data-s=\"0\">80 °C</span> or more near the bone.</li><li>If unsure, cut the biggest one to the bone after the first fry.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Is it cooked?"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Korean corn syrup (mulyeot) or light corn syrup.</li><li>Rice syrup works too — Maangchi allows it in her easier dakgangjeong.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Corn syrup"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Use <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">2 tbsp</span> crushed dried red chili instead of <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-s=\"0\">½ tbsp</span>.</p>",
   "title_html": "Spicier"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Never fill the pot more than half full, keep a lid nearby, and never put water on burning oil.</li><li>Let the oil cool completely before straining or discarding it.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Oil safety"
  }
 ],
